    content: - [x] Add `--count` flag to `iwe find`
  - [x] Locate `find` CLI argument definition and execution path
  - [x] Implement count-only output compatible with all existing filters (`--meta`, `--roots`, `--refs-to`, etc.)
  - [x] Add/update tests for `iwe find --count`
  - [x] Run `cargo build`
  - [x] Run `cargo test`
  - [x] Report changes and verification

Implemented `iwe find --count`.

Changes:
- Added `count: bool` to the `Find` CLI args in `crates/iwe/src/main.rs`.
- `find_command` now applies the existing `FindOptions` filtering path first, then if `--count` is set prints only `output.total`.
- `--count` intentionally bypasses `-f/--format` output rendering.
- Because it uses `output.total`, it reports total matches after filters and before `--limit`, consistent with existing `find` JSON semantics.

Added tests in `crates/iwe/tests/find_test.rs`:
- Basic `--count` returns only `2\n`.
- `--count` works with combined filters: `--roots`, `--refs-to`, and `--meta`.
- `--count` ignores `--limit` and `--format`, returning total matches only.

Verification:
- `cargo build` passed.
- `cargo test` passed.

Note: repo had many pre-existing modified files in `git status`; my intentional changes are limited to:
- `crates/iwe/src/main.rs`
- `crates/iwe/tests/find_test.rs`
